{:edb/db-before-t 881 :edb/db-after-t 882 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534194 50 #inst "2026-10-06T09:45:20.679Z" 13194139534194 true] [17592186105626 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281635 13194139534194 true] [17592186105626 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281643 13194139534194 true] [17592186105627 1020 #edb/ref 17592186281628 13194139534194 true] [17592186106097 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534194 true] [17592186106097 1100 "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}$. Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x$." 13194139534194 false] [17592186106097 1100 "Let $a=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186106097 1145 "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot x \\\\  & =x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x-20 & =0 \\\\ x & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186106408 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534194 true] [17592186106408 1100 "Let $a = ⟨1,-2, 5⟩$ and $b = ⟨3,-1,-1⟩$. Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b$." 13194139534194 false] [17592186106408 1100 "Let $a=⟨1,-2,5⟩$ and $b=⟨3,-1,-1⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186106408 1145 "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}b \\\\  & =⟨0,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186281629 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1089 "q-212457" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1100 "Let $a=⟨0,1,-5⟩$ and $b=⟨6,x,-2⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1113 #uuid "7b29d332-37dc-57b2-92da-0a898b30100b" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281628 1145 "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6+1\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =x+10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ x+10 & =0 \\\\ x & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281630 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281631 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281632 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281633 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186281634 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1041 "selection" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186281631 13194139534194 true] [17592186281629 1110 #uuid "1ade2e65-2f89-544d-87f3-d97153ad71a0" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281630 1034 "-5" 13194139534194 true] [17592186281630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534194 true] [1759218628163